        "margin",
        "a_c"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "a_c is the critical half-length from K_Ic. A through-wall crack of total length ~2t (half-length ~t) leaks detectably, so leak-before-break holds when the crack grows through the wall (half-length t) before reaching a_c, i.e. margin = a_c/t > 1. Use the geometry factor Y for a long through-thickness crack."
      ],
